.Dd November 4, 2026
.Dt PCH_MSI 4 loongarch64
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pch_msi
.Nd Loongson PCH MSI and MSI-X controller
.Sh SYNOPSIS
This driver is a standard part of the LoongArch kernel.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver allocates PCI MSI and MSI-X vectors on Loongson systems.
The bridge converts writes to the firmware-specified MSI address into
interrupt messages delivered through
.Xr eioic 4 .
Message data selects the absolute EIOINTC vector.
.Pp
On ACPI systems the driver obtains the message address and vector range
from the MADT MSI PIC entry.
When ACPI is absent, it attaches to a flattened device tree node with
the compatible string
.Qq loongson,pch-msi-1.0 .
The node supplies the message address in
.Va reg
and the vector range in
.Va loongson,msi-base-vec
and
.Va loongson,msi-num-vecs .
The vector range must be separate from the platform INTx vectors.
.Pp
MSI allocations use contiguous, aligned vectors.
MSI-X allocations use individual vectors.
The PCI subsystem programs the message address and data into the device;
the controller driver does not write to device BARs.
Interrupt CPU assignment is provided by
.Xr eioic 4 .
.Pp
If firmware does not describe a usable MSI controller, PCI drivers may
fall back to conventional INTx interrupts.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cpuset 1 ,
.Xr acpi 4 ,
.Xr eioic 4 ,
.Xr fdt 4 ,
.Xr pch_pic 4 ,
.Xr pci 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver was added in the LoongArch port of
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
This driver and manual page were written by
.An Hiroki Sato Aq Mt hrs@FreeBSD.org .
